.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm xtc_sync
provides async-aware synchronisation primitives that integrate
with
.Xr xtc_loop 3
scheduling: blocked acquires park the calling fiber rather than
blocking the OS thread.
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width "abort_source" -offset indent
.It Vt xtc_amutex
Async mutex.  Blocked acquires park the fiber.  Use for critical
sections held across
.Xr xtc_recv 3
or other async I/O.  Compare with
.Xr xtc_lwlock 3
which uses pthread mutex underneath
.Pq blocks the OS thread .
.Fn xtc_amutex_create
allocates a mutex;
.Fn xtc_amutex_create_ex
takes a flags word;
.Fn xtc_amutex_static
returns a process-static instance.
.Fn xtc_amutex_lock
parks until acquired or the
.Va timeout_ns
deadline elapses;
.Fn xtc_amutex_try_lock
never parks;
.Fn xtc_amutex_unlock
releases; and
.Fn xtc_amutex_destroy
frees it.
.It Vt xtc_arwlock
Async reader-writer latch (shared / exclusive).  Blocked acquires park
the fiber, exactly as
.Vt xtc_amutex ,
so a holder may park on I/O while latched and lock coupling may hold a
parent latch across a child fix without wedging a cooperative loop.
FIFO fairness keeps a read stream from starving a waiting writer.
This is the reader-writer primitive a concurrent B-tree latches its
pages with.
.Fn xtc_arwlock_create
and
.Fn xtc_arwlock_destroy
manage the object;
.Fn xtc_arwlock_rdlock
and
.Fn xtc_arwlock_wrlock
take it shared or exclusive with a
.Va timeout_ns
deadline;
.Fn xtc_arwlock_unlock
releases the current hold.
.It Vt xtc_rwlock
Reader-writer lock with writer priority, built on a pthread mutex and
condition variable: a blocked acquire blocks the OS thread (it does
NOT park the fiber).  Use
.Vt xtc_arwlock
instead on the hot path of an event loop.
.Fn xtc_rwlock_create ,
.Fn xtc_rwlock_destroy ,
.Fn xtc_rwlock_rdlock ,
.Fn xtc_rwlock_wrlock ,
and
.Fn xtc_rwlock_unlock
mirror the async variant.
.It Vt xtc_notify
A 0-or-1 latch.
.Fn xtc_notify_create
and
.Fn xtc_notify_destroy
manage the object.  Producers
.Fn xtc_notify_signal ;
consumers
.Fn xtc_notify_wait
until signalled.  Useful for one-shot ready signals.
.It Vt xtc_sem
Counting semaphore.
.Fn xtc_sem_create
takes an
.Va initial
count;
.Fn xtc_sem_destroy
frees it.
.Fn xtc_sem_post
adds
.Va n
permits;
.Fn xtc_sem_acquire
takes
.Va n
permits, parking until available or the
.Va timeout_ns
deadline;
.Fn xtc_sem_try_acquire
never parks; and
.Fn xtc_sem_count
reports the current permit count.
.It Vt xtc_barrier
Synchronisation point:
.Va n
participants created by
.Fn xtc_barrier_create
call
.Fn xtc_barrier_wait
until all have arrived; then all proceed.
.Fn xtc_barrier_destroy
frees it.
.It Vt xtc_gate
A counting gate.
.Fn xtc_gate_create
and
.Fn xtc_gate_destroy
manage the object.
.Fn xtc_gate_enter
and
.Fn xtc_gate_leave
bracket in-flight work;
.Fn xtc_gate_close
rejects new entrants;
.Fn xtc_gate_drain
parks until the in-flight count reaches zero or the
.Va timeout_ns
deadline; and
.Fn xtc_gate_count
reports the number of active occupants.
.It Vt xtc_abort_source
Cancellation token.
.Fn xtc_abort_source_create
and
.Fn xtc_abort_source_destroy
manage the source.  Initiator calls
.Fn xtc_abort_source_fire
with a
.Va reason
to signal cancellation;
.Fn xtc_abort_source_token
hands out a token participants poll with
.Fn xtc_abort_token_is_aborted
and
.Fn xtc_abort_token_reason .
Used to wire timeout / shutdown into long-running
operations cooperatively.
.El
.Pp
All primitives are thread-safe.  All blocked-acquire paths park
the calling fiber via
.Xr xtc_proc_wait_fd 3
or directly into the loop's wait queue, so the OS thread is free
to run other work.
.Sh CHOOSING
.Bl -bullet -compact -offset indent
.It
For database-style transactional locking with deadlock detection:
.Xr xtc_lockmgr 3 .
.It
For short critical sections inside one xtc_loop:
.Xr xtc_lwlock 3 .
.It
For read-mostly state with wait-free readers:
.Xr xtc_lrlock 3
or
.Xr xtc_rcu 3 .
.It
For "wait until N producers have all signalled":
.Vt xtc_barrier
or
.Vt xtc_sem .
.It
For cancellation propagation:
.Vt xtc_abort_source .
.El
